{
  "title": "Piano Practice",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Read",
      "lines": [
        "Notes scroll right to",
        "left on a treble staff.",
        "Play the pad as the note",
        "crosses the line.",
        "",
        "On time: the notehead",
        "turns into a circle.",
        "Missed: it turns into",
        "an X.",
        "",
        "A circle also marks where",
        "you actually played. In",
        "time, it lands on the",
        "note as one mark. Late,",
        "you see two and the gap",
        "is your error.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops and names",
        "it on screen. With Guide",
        "pads on, the pad you",
        "need pulses white.",
        "",
        "Miss a note and the",
        "scroll stops on it. The X",
        "stays by the line however",
        "far ahead you are reading."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Guess",
      "lines": [
        "Three extra modes, from",
        "the top of the exercise",
        "list.",
        "Guess: notes / chords",
        "One note or chord sits",
        "still on the staff, named",
        "below it, until you play",
        "it. No clock, no timing.",
        "",
        "Hear: notes / chords",
        "The same, but you hear it",
        "instead of seeing it. The",
        "staff shows a ? until you",
        "play it right, then it",
        "reveals what it was.",
        "",
        "Both drill finding a",
        "pitch on the grid, which",
        "is its own skill: the",
        "pads go up in fifths, so",
        "the same note sits in",
        "several places.",
        "",
        "A chord must be held all",
        "at once. Part of it down",
        "is not yet a mistake.",
        "",
        "Pick: notes / chords",
        "A pad lights and you name",
        "it, choosing one of three",
        "with the jog. Click to",
        "answer. The other two are",
        "near misses - a semitone",
        "away, or the same chord",
        "root with another quality",
        "- so a rough sense of",
        "high or low will not do.",
        "",
        "This is the only mode",
        "that goes pad to name,",
        "and the only one you can",
        "do without playing.",
        "",
        "PLAY   hear it",
        "REC    skip it",
        "BACK   back to the list",
        "",
        "Half tones adds the black",
        "notes to the note pools.",
        "On by default: they are",
        "the hard ones to find.",
        "",
        "Chords: triads asks the",
        "diatonic triads of the",
        "key. types asks a chosen",
        "quality instead - dim,",
        "aug, sus, 6, 7, maj7, m7,",
        "m7b5, dim7, add9 - and",
        "names it on screen, so",
        "you read the symbol and",
        "play it.",
        "",
        "The answer is never lit",
        "on the pads. Guide pads is",
        "a playing aid, not a",
        "hint for a quiz."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rounds",
      "lines": [
        "A quiz is a round of 20",
        "prompts (10/20/30 in",
        "settings, or endless).",
        "",
        "The clock starts on your",
        "first press, not when the",
        "screen appears. A prompt",
        "waits until you get it",
        "right, so a wrong answer",
        "costs you time rather",
        "than a penalty - the same",
        "way a typing test treats",
        "a typo.",
        "",
        "The result is correct",
        "answers per minute, and",
        "whether it beat your best.",
        "",
        "Progress, at the top of",
        "the list, plots how one",
        "drill has developed. Jog",
        "changes drill. Rates only",
        "compare within a drill -",
        "hearing 7th chords is not",
        "naming a white note.",
        "",
        "endless records nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Play",
      "lines": [
        "PLAY   listen. The",
        "  exercise plays itself",
        "  and the pads light up",
        "  as it goes, so you can",
        "  watch it before you",
        "  try it. Nothing scored.",
        "REC    practice. You",
        "  play it, it scores you.",
        "",
        "Both pulse when ready.",
        "The one that is running",
        "goes solid.",
        "",
        "JOG    pick, in the list",
        "CLICK  open the list",
        "MENU   open the list",
        "BACK   up one level",
        "SHIFT + BACK   close",
        "",
        "shift + jog: settings",
        "",
        "Four beats count you in,",
        "counted on screen."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sound",
      "lines": [
        "The module has its own",
        "piano. It is the default",
        "and needs no setup: no",
        "track, no instrument, no",
        "MIDI channel to match.",
        "It mixes in alongside",
        "whatever else Move is",
        "playing.",
        "",
        "MIDI out can send",
        "elsewhere instead:",
        "track  a Move track,",
        "  on the MIDI ch below",
        "  (all = every channel)",
        "USB    the USB-A port",
        "trk+USB  both of those",
        "",
        "Closing silences the",
        "piano and every channel",
        "on both MIDI routes,",
        "then waits for it to",
        "drain before letting go.",
        "SHIFT + BACK closes",
        "from anywhere."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Settings",
      "lines": [
        "SHIFT + CLICK opens",
        "settings. CLICK a row to",
        "edit it, turn to change,",
        "CLICK again when done.",
        "",
        "Wait stops the scroll at",
        "a note until you play it.",
        "On by default.",
        "",
        "Grace is how late still",
        "counts as in time, as a",
        "fraction of a beat. The",
        "scroll only stops past",
        "it, so a small wobble",
        "never breaks the rhythm.",
        "A note waited for still",
        "scores a miss.",
        "",
        "Guide pads lights the",
        "pad you need next. Off",
        "by default so you read",
        "rather than follow. It",
        "does nothing in the",
        "guessing modes.",
        "",
        "Any octave accepts the",
        "right note in the wrong",
        "register.",
        "",
        "Exercises live in the",
        "exercises folder. Add a",
        "JSON file and list it",
        "in index.json."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
